id: pm-oq893h
title: "POSIX recovery commands are not paste-safe in interactive bash or zsh: a ! inside the double-quoted form triggers history expansion"
description: "Found 2026-11-24 while implementing the shell dialects for pm-kjoudp and GH-1774. The posix renderer in src/core/shared/command-line.ts escapes double quote, backslash, dollar and backtick inside double quotes, which is complete for sh -c and for scripts. An interactive bash with histexpand on (the default) or zsh still expands an exclamation mark inside double quotes: a pasted retry such as pm create --title \"Fix crash!now\" fails with event not found, or substitutes an earlier command. Single quotes suppress history expansion in both shells. Duplicate check: searched history expansion, exclamation, interactive bash, recovery quoting; pm-kjoudp and pm-gh1774 cover cmd.exe and PowerShell only."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,posix,recovery
